data/review-queue.json
# hook c192 (2026-10-09, the Janitor's D466 / the adversarial review's A02 rider): the museum's BUILD INPUTS are not served.
# Nothing is moved and nothing is deleted - every one of these stays in the repository, where the builders, the validators and
# the gate read it from disk. No served page fetches any of them: every data load on a served page goes through
# MuseumList.fetchJSON, whose callers are 30 literal /data/<name>.json paths plus search.html's own FILES array, and a grep of
# every *.html/*.js/*.mjs/*.css in the tree finds these names only in five character pages' PROSE citations.
# data/external-figures.json is NOT here on purpose: search.html loads it by name, so no literal path names it.
# r2-sync matches these entries against the relative path (scripts/r2-sync.mjs isExcluded), and walkTree tests directories too,
# so the one data/shards line prunes all 15,457 shard files.
data/shards
data/wanted.json
data/documents.json
data/affiliations.json
data/attestors.json
data/promotion-epitaph-authorship.json
data/promotion-style-families.json
data/stip-codes.json
data/stipulation-families.json
data/style-families.json
